Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 06:32:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] fix(search): enforce fixed cards and characters in finale
 searches

The grouped finale solvers only model a leader, so fixed cards and every
fixed character after the first were dropped silently. JP #218 now takes
the finale path, so pinned cards disappeared from its decks; #180 already
behaved this way in 0.0.14.

- Keep the grouped solvers for requests with no fixed card and at most
  one fixed character; send every other finale request to the slot-aware
  DFS, whose leader is fixed slot 0.
- When a forced leader is not slot 0, rewrite the fixed cards as fixed
  characters (the pool keeps only that card of each such character) with
  the leader first, so DFS enforces the leader and every pin.
- Build the DFS bounds from the leader's finale support deck instead of
  the world_bloom_character_id fallback, which could prune the optimum.
- Skip the finale warm start that ignores fixed slots when slots are set.
- Test every constraint shape against brute force for Score Multi/Solo
  and Mysekai with per-leader support decks.

Unconstrained, forced-leader-only and single fixed character finale
requests keep the grouped path, so this commit does not change them.
